A||N||11||DaRkLoRD||wheel "mags"?||||5||
Z||000000||DaRkLoRD||11-24-2000||01:15 PM||||Time for another dumb question.. what's a "wheel mag"? I've heard the term mag wheels before, and AFAIK it's short for magnesium wheels..<BR>I got an email from a guy asking: <P>"My friend wrote this email, he is having a 86 Fiero GT and he just wanted to know wich wheel mags can fit on his car.<BR>Hope you can help him"<P>is this guy asking what size wheels will fit on the Fiero??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||11-24-2000||02:22 PM||||As Microsoft's grammer checker would say... order of words, consider revising.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||11-24-2000||02:23 PM||||Sounds to me like he's talking about a "Mag Wheel" &lt;Magnesium&gt; Just as you said?? His question must be what size will fit his car.<P>Wheel Mag, is that what you call it in Canada??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. Some people that are not so into cars will call all after market wheels<BR>Mags?<P>Good luck helping him!<P>DXR_DAD||||reg||3
Z||000003||DaRkLoRD||11-24-2000||02:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DXR_DAD:<BR><B>Wheel Mag, is that what you call it in Canada??   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. Some people that are not so into cars will call all after market wheels Mags?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>If that's what we called them here in Canada, I wouldn't have the problem of not knowing what this guy meant..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I'll just send him to tirerack.com or something, that's what I used to find the wheels I want.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> (ASA JS5, 17x7.5)<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||12
Z||000004||terryk||11-24-2000||02:39 PM||||From *magnesium* wheel, but it's become a generic term for alloy wheels which would actually be an alloy of magnesium and aluminum, but most are aluminum now. Might be some magnesium in there anyway.<P>Got that? Quiz on Monday.<P>Do yourself a favor. You are a million times better off using a GM factory alloy wheel that you like rather than an aftermarket alloy wheel. I've fought the balancing of a few aftermarket wheels and unless you are will to pay $250+ for each one (high quality), the GM factory wheels are hands- down the best quality. The centering is horrible too on the cheaper wheels. <P>Anyone have a set of Olds 16" wheels in 5x115mm? <P>IMHO||||reg||1
Z||000005||DaRkLoRD||11-24-2000||03:04 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by terryk:<BR><B>From *magnesium* wheel, but it's become a generic term for alloy wheels which would actually be an alloy of magnesium and aluminum, but most are aluminum now. Might be some magnesium in there anyway.<P>Got that? Quiz on Monday.<BR></B><P>heh.. if my Engineering Materials (aka metallurgy) prof were to have explained that, it would have taken 2 hours and we still wouldn't know what's going on.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><B><BR>Do yourself a favor. You are a million times better off using a GM factory alloy wheel that you like rather than an aftermarket alloy wheel. I've fought the balancing of a few aftermarket wheels and unless you are will to pay $250+ for each one (high quality), the GM factory wheels are hands- down the best quality. The centering is horrible too on the cheaper wheels. <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'd prefer a set of 16" 2000 Grand Prix wheels, but they don't fit the Fiero.. and IMHO, a lot of the stock GM wheels are just plain ugly.. that's why aftermarket wheels exist.. LOL.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> I can understand what you mean about quality though. <P>new question.. has anyone ever had any problems with aftermarket wheels?<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000006||Philphine||11-24-2000||03:23 PM||||maybe if you're in canada this person speaks french primarily and didn't translate well.<P>never had problems with after market wheels except once getting some tires mounted on some keystone classics (for a '73 grand prix) one of the wheels cracked in the center. still used the wheel but the center cap barely went on.<P>i'm more curiuos as to weather any one has used wheel adapters on a fiero. i've got some wheels i might like to try on mine but i need to change bolt pattern and possibly some back space. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||DaRkLoRD||11-24-2000||03:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Philphine:<BR><B>maybe if you're in canada this person speaks french primarily and didn't translate well.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I think that's what might have happened, as the person's last name was french..<P>I was pretty sure what he meant, but I just wanted to clarify in case "mag" meant something else I wasn't aware of.<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000008||terryk||11-24-2000||08:12 PM||||Yeah. I had problems with AR's. Spin balancing off the car was a waste. <P>Maybe wheel mags are wheel magnifiers, those lenses you put on your wheels to make them look bigger. Kinda like X-ray glasses. <p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 11-24-2000).]||||reg||1
